<!-- PIPE_POLES_BUILD_SAG_WITH_SUBSTANCE phase 4 (design/RimMandrake/flowworks_pipes_across_pits_design_2026-10-20.md §P3):
     the pipe pole. Owner, answer 1: "Pipes get a version of the power pole: supports that provide a somewhat saggy hose between
     them. Same mechanics, just much thicker and less flexible. Same art variation."
     * Mechanics: a Gimme Some Slack aerial anchor of kind Pipe (CompProperties_AerialAnchor + AerialAnchorExtension lineKind Pipe):
       GSS's links, auto-link, span mesh, cut / re-string and fallen halves, with no power comp (a pipe span never joins a power
       net), one strand, no drip loop, no sway. Range and sag are FlowWorks Mod Settings (pipePoleMaxSpan, pipePoleSag) handed to
       GSS at startup (Source/Machinery/RM_PipePoles.cs). MayRequire GSS on every def here: without GSS nothing here loads.
     * Ground: solid ground only, never a bridge deck, a pit cover or a dug square (review answer 8): LineKind PipePole on the
       phase-1 gates (placement, frame completion, auto-rebuild; a committed dig KILLS the pole so its spans fall) plus
       PlaceWorker_PipePole (always, whatever the crossing switch). A span is never walking ground, a deck or pawn topology.
     * Art: NONE commissioned (owner: no pole art before LINE_WIDTH_JUDGE_ARMS_NOT_INCLUDED). Stand-ins that exist: the GSS mast of
       the same look, tinted steel-blue so a pipe pole never reads as a power mast. Art contract (installed by `art install` once
       judged; then each style's texPath below is pointed at it): RimMandrake/FlowWorks/PipePole/<Look>/PipePole (pole, 2x4 like
       the mast) and RimMandrake/FlowWorks/PipePole/<Look>/PipeSpan (span strip, looked up SILENTLY by GSS's PipeMats until it
       exists; until then the span draws the look's wire at the pipe's 0.22-cell width). PipeSpan.png INSTALLED 2026-10-22 (D5, joints
       study): derived from each look's own ground pipe atlas by art_source/PipeSpan/make_pipe_span.py, no new design; the pole stays
       the tinted stand-in until LINE_WIDTH_JUDGE_ARMS_NOT_INCLUDED.
     * Looks: the pipe's four (PipeStyles.Looks), picked on the build button through PipeLook (RM_PipePole_<Look>). -->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.gimmesomeslack">
    <defName>RM_PipePole</defName>
    <label>pipe pole</label>
    <description>A stout steel post with a saddle clamp at the top. Two pipe poles hang a stiff overhead pipe between them, so a pipe line can cross a pit, trench, canal or moat without touching it. Poles must stand on solid ground under open sky, never on a bridge deck, a pit cover or a dug square; the pipe overhead is not walkable. Digging out a pole's square knocks it down. Pick its look on the build button.</description>
    <thingClass>Building</thingClass>
    <category>Building</category>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>PassThroughOnly</passability>
    <pathCost>14</pathCost>
    <fillPercent>0.15</fillPercent>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <drawerType>MapMeshAndRealTime</drawerType>
    <drawOffscreen>true</drawOffscreen>
    <drawPlaceWorkersWhileSelected>true</drawPlaceWorkersWhileSelected>
    <designationCategory>VCHE_PipeNetworks</designationCategory>
    <constructEffect>ConstructMetal</constructEffect>
    <terrainAffordanceNeeded>Light</terrainAffordanceNeeded>
    <minifiedDef>MinifiedThing</minifiedDef>
    <thingCategories><li>BuildingsMisc</li></thingCategories>
    <leaveResourcesWhenKilled>false</leaveResourcesWhenKilled>
    <soundImpactDefault>BulletImpact_Metal</soundImpactDefault>
    <repairEffect>Repair</repairEffect>
    <filthLeaving>Filth_RubbleBuilding</filthLeaving>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>RimMandrake/GimmeSomeSlack/Aerial/Styles/Scrapper/AerialMast</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(2,4)</drawSize>
      <drawOffset>(0,0,1.5)</drawOffset>
      <color>(170,182,196)</color>
      <shadowData><volume>(0.25, 1.6, 0.25)</volume></shadowData>
      <damageData><rect>(0.3,0.1,0.4,0.8)</rect></damageData>
    </graphicData>
    <uiIconScale>0.9</uiIconScale>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>250</MaxHitPoints>
      <WorkToBuild>800</WorkToBuild>
      <Flammability>0.2</Flammability>
      <Mass>12</Mass>
    </statBases>
    <costList>
      <Steel>40</Steel>
    </costList>
    <building>
      <ai_chillDestination>false</ai_chillDestination>
      <expandHomeArea>false</expandHomeArea>
    </building>
    <placeWorkers>
      <li>PlaceWorker_NotUnderRoof</li>
      <li>RimMandrake.FlowWorks.Machinery.PlaceWorker_PipePole</li>
      <li>RimMandrake.GimmeSomeSlack.Aerial.PlaceWorker_AerialRange</li>
    </placeWorkers>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Styleable" />
      <!-- no CompProperties_Power: a pipe pole is never a power building, so no power net ever visits it -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.GimmeSomeSlack.Aerial.CompProperties_AerialAnchor" />
      <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.Machinery.CompProperties_PipePoleReadout" />   <!-- P9 readout: does its span carry the net -->
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.GimmeSomeSlack.Aerial.AerialAnchorExtension">
        <lineKind>Pipe</lineKind>
        <maxLinks>3</maxLinks>   <!-- PROVISIONAL: a run in, a run out, one branch -->
        <attachZ>2.66</attachZ>  <!-- the stand-in mast's crossarm height; re-measure from the pole art when it lands -->
        <insulatorSpread>0</insulatorSpread>
        <spanWidth>0.14</spanWidth>   <!-- RM_PipePoleMath.SpanWidthCells: the ground pipe atlas's girth (PIPE_GIRTH_TUNE_HALF_AS_THICK, 2026-10-21); PipeSpan.png (D5, 2026-10-22) is the look's pipe filling its strip, so the span draws exactly this wide -->
        <spanTexPath>RimMandrake/FlowWorks/PipePole/{look}/PipeSpan</spanTexPath>
      </li>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.Machinery.RM_LineKindExtension">
        <kind>PipePole</kind>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </ThingDef>

